        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पठिष्यामि",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पठिष्यामि — paṭhiṣyāmi — means “I will read” or “I will study.” Learn the complete form; its future stem is given, not guessed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "Taken Apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पठिष्यामि (paṭhiṣyāmi) comes from the root पठ् (paṭh), “read, recite.” Its future here is पठिष्य- (paṭhiṣya-), followed by first-person -आमि. Whitney, Sanskrit Grammar §§932–935, describes the Sanskrit s-future and the -iṣya- / -sya- formation used here."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
