              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Give the three future forms only: I will go, I will do, I will read. (Gamiṣyāmi; kariṣyāmi; paṭhiṣyāmi.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "SA-C264-first-person-future-retrieval",
      "sequence": 15690,
      "title": "Say what you will do",
      "headword": "(first-person future retrieval)",
      "romanization": "",
      "gloss": "independently say a near-term plan with a taught future form",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:62213892783e416e",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is a first-person singular checkpoint. Every answer tells your own near-term plan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice — independent retrieval",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": true,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s each]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "You plan to travel tomorrow. Say when and what you will do. — śvaḥ gamiṣyāmi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: You plan to travel tomorrow. Say when and what you will do. — *śvaḥ gamiṣyāmi*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "You plan to study tomorrow. Say when and what you will do. — śvaḥ paṭhiṣyāmi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: You plan to study tomorrow. Say when and what you will do. — *śvaḥ paṭhiṣyāmi*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "You plan to do the work the day after tomorrow. — paraśvaḥ kāryaṃ kariṣyāmi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: You plan to do the work the day after tomorrow. — *paraśvaḥ kāryaṃ kariṣyāmi*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "Choose a different one of the three actions and make your own tomorrow plan.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: Choose a different one of the three actions and make your own tomorrow plan.]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: the boundary",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "These three complete forms make a useful first-person singular ramp. This is not a complete future paradigm. Second person, dual, and plural forms, and the future stems of other roots, wait for later lessons."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Without a model, say one true or imagined plan for tomorrow with गमिष्यामि, करिष्यामि (kariṣyāmi), or पठिष्यामि (paṭhiṣyāmi)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
